WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.164
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.464 --> 00:00:08.897
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.197 --> 00:00:15.124
Unit eleven: Working in a Team. In this unit, you will share opinions and work together in a team.

4
00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:16.758
Team.

5
00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:20.282
Team means a group of people who work together.

6
00:00:20.582 --> 00:00:22.314
Our team won the science fair.

7
00:00:23.014 --> 00:00:25.365
Your turn. Say: Team.

8
00:00:28.065 --> 00:00:28.787
Team.

9
00:00:29.783 --> 00:00:30.645
Role.

10
00:00:31.345 --> 00:00:33.600
Role means the job a person has in a group.

11
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.621
My role is to take notes.

12
00:00:36.321 --> 00:00:38.822
Your turn. Say: Role.

13
00:00:41.522 --> 00:00:42.198
Role.

14
00:00:43.183 --> 00:00:43.894
Leader.

15
00:00:44.594 --> 00:00:46.791
Leader means the person who guides a group.

16
00:00:47.091 --> 00:00:48.777
Sokha is our team leader.

17
00:00:49.477 --> 00:00:52.246
Your turn. Say: Leader.

18
00:00:54.946 --> 00:00:55.726
Leader.

19
00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:57.428
Listen.

20
00:00:58.128 --> 00:01:01.091
Listen means to pay attention to what someone says.

21
00:01:01.391 --> 00:01:03.483
A good team member listens to others.

22
00:01:04.183 --> 00:01:07.068
Your turn. Say: Listen.

23
00:01:09.768 --> 00:01:10.618
Listen.

24
00:01:11.617 --> 00:01:12.444
Share.

25
00:01:13.144 --> 00:01:16.095
Share means to tell others your ideas or give them things.

26
00:01:16.395 --> 00:01:18.151
Share your ideas with the team.

27
00:01:18.851 --> 00:01:21.619
Your turn. Say: Share.

28
00:01:24.319 --> 00:01:24.949
Share.

29
00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:26.777
Agree.

30
00:01:27.477 --> 00:01:29.558
Agree means to have the same opinion.

31
00:01:29.858 --> 00:01:30.987
I agree with you.

32
00:01:31.687 --> 00:01:34.525
Your turn. Say: Agree.

33
00:01:37.225 --> 00:01:37.924
Agree.

34
00:01:38.917 --> 00:01:39.732
Disagree.

35
00:01:40.432 --> 00:01:42.617
Disagree means to have a different opinion.

36
00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:45.497
I disagree, but I respect your idea.

37
00:01:46.197 --> 00:01:48.548
Your turn. Say: Disagree.

38
00:01:51.248 --> 00:01:52.156
Disagree.

39
00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:53.780
Goal.

40
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.885
Goal means what a team wants to achieve.

41
00:01:57.185 --> 00:01:59.464
Our goal is to finish the poster today.

42
00:02:00.164 --> 00:02:02.143
Your turn. Say: Goal.

43
00:02:04.843 --> 00:02:05.484
Goal.

44
00:02:06.483 --> 00:02:08.506
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:08.806 --> 00:02:11.758
Sreypich, your team must make a poster about recycling.

46
00:02:13.050 --> 00:02:15.282
I think we should draw a big recycling bin.

47
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:19.456
Your friend wants to use photos. Do you agree?

48
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.912
I agree because photos are clear and real.

49
00:02:24.217 --> 00:02:25.427
Who is the leader?

50
00:02:26.717 --> 00:02:30.077
Dara is the leader. My role is to write the words.

51
00:02:31.383 --> 00:02:34.764
Grammar focus: I agree and I disagree because.

52
00:02:35.064 --> 00:02:37.029
I agree because it's a good idea.

53
00:02:37.329 --> 00:02:41.746
Always give a reason. It's polite to say 'I disagree' calmly and respectfully.

54
00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.472
Now read and listen. Our Science Project.

55
00:02:45.772 --> 00:02:49.153
Last month, our class worked in teams for a science project.

56
00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.761
Each person had a role, and Sokha was our leader.

57
00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.421
We listened to each other and shared our ideas.

58
00:02:58.717 --> 00:03:02.191
Sometimes we disagreed, but we always gave reasons.

59
00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:05.796
We reached our goal because we worked as a team.

60
00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:09.550
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:12.070
I disagree blank it's too difficult.

62
00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.919
A, because. B, so. C, who.

63
00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:22.090
The answer is A: because.

64
00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:25.850
The job a person has in a group is a blank.

65
00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:28.979
A, role. B, goal. C, team.

66
00:03:32.983 --> 00:03:35.006
The answer is A: role.

67
00:03:36.517 --> 00:03:38.458
To have the same opinion is to blank.

68
00:03:38.758 --> 00:03:42.493
A, agree. B, disagree. C, listen.

69
00:03:46.483 --> 00:03:48.564
The answer is A: agree.

70
00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:52.679
Now it's your turn to speak. What makes a good team?

71
00:03:57.979 --> 00:04:04.393
A good team has a fair leader, and everyone has a role. I think listening is important because everyone's ideas matter.

72
00:04:04.693 --> 00:04:06.368
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:07.383 --> 00:04:12.927
Great work today! You learned eight new words and i agree and i disagree because.

74
00:04:13.227 --> 00:04:16.947
Today's value is teamwork. We can do more when we work together.

75
00:04:17.247 --> 00:04:20.039
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

76
00:04:20.339 --> 00:04:23.154
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

